      "skills/method/references/upstream.md": "# Upstream provenance\n\n- Repository: [K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills](https://github.com/K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills)\n- Pinned commit: `7eb9c23c32ecf7f8c19cb45ded3150534ccefe6a`\n- Selected source: `skills/research-grants/SKILL.md`\n- Pinned raw source: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills/7eb9c23c32ecf7f8c19cb45ded3150534ccefe6a/skills/research-grants/SKILL.md`\n- Pinned source SHA-256 verified 2026-08-11: `462a32fa85d11dcba4363b4f955bc6ec069ecd765f5519bbcdc7473a10f6507d`.\n- License: MIT; full notice is saved in `upstream-license.txt`.\n- Verification date: 2026-08-11. The saved notice exactly matches `LICENSE.md` at the pinned commit after line-ending normalization. Reverify the pinned source and repository license only when changing the adaptation; verify every live solicitation independently from current funder materials.\n- Bounded concepts adapted: requirement-first proposal structure, review-criteria traceability, theory-of-change and evidence organization, feasibility, budget justification, milestones, and broader-impact evidence.\n- Explicitly excluded: agency-specific current-rule claims, image-service calls, bundled scripts, autonomous research or submission behavior, fabricated proposal content, funder contact, signature, certification, and organizational commitment authority.\n\nThis package is an OpenCorvus-specific bounded adaptation. The local Skill and assets are the runtime source of truth; upstream supplies no current solicitation, legal, tax, safeguarding, or accounting conclusion.\n",
      "skills/method/SKILL.md": "---\nname: nonprofit-grant-operations-method\ndescription: Prepare traceable nonprofit grant opportunity, proposal, and post-award readiness packs from funder requirements, theory of change, program evidence, indicators, budget bases, allowability questions, match and indirect-cost assumptions, milestones, safeguarding, controls, and reporting duties. Use for go/no-go, proposal development, reviewer response, or delivery planning without eligibility, submission, certification, spending, or organizational commitment authority.\n---\n\n# Nonprofit Grant Operations Method\n\n## Freeze the opportunity\n\n1. Register the solicitation identifier, issuer, version, all amendments, publication/retrieved dates, deadline/time zone, submission channel, proposed period, applicant entity, decision owner, data boundary, and excluded actions.\n2. Atomize eligibility, mandatory, evaluation, budget, reporting, safeguarding, data, partnership, and post-award requirements in [the requirement matrix](assets/funder-requirement-traceability-matrix.md). Preserve exact page/section or stable URL.\n3. Separate funder text, analyst paraphrase, approved organizational fact, draft proposal claim, projection, partner assertion, and unresolved question.\n\n## Build program evidence and a testable logic model\n\n1. Trace authorized need evidence to problem, inputs, activities, outputs, short/intermediate/long outcomes, assumptions, external factors, and risks in [the logic-model register](assets/logic-model-and-indicator-register.md).\n2. Keep outputs (delivered products/services) distinct from outcomes (changes). Treat attribution as a claim requiring design evidence.\n3. Define each indicator with numerator, denominator, unit, population, collection method, frequency, baseline, target-as-proposal, disaggregation/privacy limits, source, date, and owner.\n4. Test capacity, partner status, beneficiary evidence, safeguarding, data collection burden, and causal links. Qualify or remove unsupported claims.\n\n## Rebuild budget and post-award controls\n\n1. Calculate each budget line from a declared basis such as quantity × rate × period. State currency, exchange-rate source/date, source/version, and uncertainty.\n2. Reconcile direct + indirect + permitted contingency to request total. Reconcile cash and in-kind match separately; never assume uncommitted match or partner funding.\n3. Map each cost to activity/output and exact rule. Label allowability, indirect-cost, tax, legal, and match treatment as review questions unless supported by authorized documentation.\n4. Map cash timing, procurement, subaward, restricted-fund, timesheet, reporting, evidence retention, audit, safeguarding, and closeout controls in [the budget/control register](assets/budget-and-post-award-control-register.md).\n\n## Join proposal and delivery readiness\n\nRequire all three independent branches and compatible solicitation versions, periods, currencies, and populations. Map every requirement to evidence, claim/attachment, owner, reviewer, and status. Map activities to budget, milestones, outputs, indicators, reports, and controls. Preserve disagreement and absent evidence in [the grant delivery plan](assets/grant-delivery-plan.md); never manufacture completeness.\n\n## Authority and stop boundary\n\nNever fabricate need, impact, outcomes, partners, beneficiary facts, consent, match, rates, or commitments; determine eligibility or legal/tax compliance; sign, certify, submit, contact a funder, accept an award, or approve spending. Stop on uncertain solicitation version, unresolved mandatory requirement, unsafe beneficiary data, missing safeguarding owner, unsupported partner/impact claim, irreconcilable budget, or unclear allowability/indirect-cost treatment. Require authorized program, monitoring/evaluation, grants, finance, legal/tax, safeguarding, privacy, procurement, partner, executive, and funder-facing review.\n\n## Assets\n\n- Trace solicitation clauses in [Funder Requirement Traceability Matrix](assets/funder-requirement-traceability-matrix.md).\n- Define the causal chain and measures in [Logic Model and Indicator Register](assets/logic-model-and-indicator-register.md).\n- Reconcile money and controls in [Budget and Post-Award Control Register](assets/budget-and-post-award-control-register.md).\n- Join the proposal and mobilization decision in [Grant Delivery Plan](assets/grant-delivery-plan.md).\n\n## Adaptation boundary\n\nApply only the bounded concepts recorded in [upstream provenance](references/upstream.md). Do not invoke upstream scripts, current-rule claims, global agent protocols, or authority excluded by this package.\n",
